\paragraph{Contributions.}
\begin{enumerate}[nosep,leftmargin=*]
    \item \textbf{Failure mode identification.} We identify CIVO as specific to imagination-based actor-critic with temporal conditioning. Factorial analysis isolates trained $\dt$-embedding $+$ multi-rate exposure as jointly sufficient (5/7 locomotion seeds, 0/16 controls). The NVE $\geq 2.0\times$ threshold achieves perfect classification ($n{=}36$; AUROC${=}1.000$, F1${=}1.000$; 9 CIVO-positive vs.\ 27 non-CIVO); cross-environment validation confirms specificity to multi-joint locomotion (\S\ref{sec:discussion}).
    \item \textbf{Systematic intervention hierarchy.} Seven interventions across four levels (gradient, output, representation, architecture) fail to reliably eliminate CIVO; dual critics converge in pure imagination ($\rho > 0.999$), so Double Q pessimism vanishes. Only wide dual-critic (min $+$ increased capacity) achieves partial prevention (3/4 seeds)---the sole positive result across all tested approaches.
    \item \textbf{Mechanism analysis.} Frozen embeddings never trigger CIVO (0/16 vs.\ 5/7 trained, $p < 0.001$), establishing embedding \emph{learning}---not conditioning architecture---as causal. A $2{\times}2$ critic factorial dissects the architectural result: min-aggregation drives recovery, increased capacity enables prevention, and their combination is the minimum sufficient condition.
\end{enumerate}

