\subsection{F3--F5: Causal Ablation and Cross-Environment Validation}
\label{sec:f3f5_summary}

Trained $\dt$-embedding triggers CIVO in 5/7 multi-joint locomotion seeds vs.\ 0/16 frozen or removed controls ($p < 0.001$; Table~\ref{tab:three_way_emb}); a random-policy decomposition attributes ${\approx}36\%$ of the effect to dynamics bias and ${\approx}64\%$ to actor exploitation (Appendix~\ref{sec:civo_mechanism}). Cross-environment validation on three ManiSkill tasks shows comparable value-ratio transients ($4$--$11\times$) with frozen controls matching, ruling out $\dt$-embedding causation (Table~\ref{tab:cross_domain}); CIVO is specific to multi-joint locomotion. Full factorial analysis in Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_factorial}.

